                <head>Annex</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vote in General Assembly</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Sixth Session</hi>) <hi rendition="#small-caps">on
                        Two Covenant Issue</hi></p>
                <p>The resolution calling on the Commission on Human Rights to draft two Covenants
                    on Human Rights was adopted by the General Assembly in plenary on February 5,
                    1952 by a vote of 27 to 20 with 3 abstentions. This vote was not a roll-call
                    one, and it therefore is difficult to state exactly which countries voted for
                    and against the resolution. There was, however, a roll-call vote in the plenary
                    session of the General Assembly the same day on an amendment submitted by Chile
                    calling for one covenant. This amendment was rejected 25 to 29 with 4
                    abstentions. The vote on this amendment was as follows: <table cols="3"
                        rows="30">
